            <ArticleTitle>A perforated sigmoid diverticulum abscess difficult to differentiate from an ovarian tumor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>276-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a perforated sigmoid diverticulum abscess that was difficult to differentiate from an ovarian tumor. A 53-year-old woman was diagnosed with an ovarian tumor, but laparotomy revealed a perforated sigmoid diverticulum abscess and appendicitis, with normal ovaries.</AbstractText>
